<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n105450" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρῐχόω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>furnish</i> or <i>cover with hair,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				5.149
			</span></i> :—
				Pass.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τριχοῦσθαι τὸ γένειον</span>
			<i>to get</i> or <i>have</i> a beard, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>APo.</u>
				96a10
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				12.379
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Adam.
				2.37
			</span></i>; <i>to be mixed with hairs,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πηλὸς τετριχωμένος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thphr.
					<u>CP</u>
					1.6.7
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Polyaen.
				6.3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>unravel</i> a thread, <i><span class="en">
				Heliod.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				47.17.2
			</span></i> (
				Pass.
			). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τριχῶσαι: θάψαι,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i> (perh. cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταρχύω</span>).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
